msgid "About the bridge"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The XRPL EVM Sidechain bridge runs on Axelar Amplifier — Axelar's "
"framework for\n"
"      connecting new chains to its interchain network. On the XRPL side, "
"a single\n"
"      account holds the SignerList that authorizes every bridge "
"operation; that account\n"
"      is the receiving address for user-initiated bridge transfers and "
"the signing\n"
"      account for messages relayed back from the Sidechain."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A bridge transfer starts as a regular XRPL <code>Payment</code> "
"transaction sent to\n"
"      that account, with hex-encoded memos carrying the destination "
"chain, contract,\n"
"      and ABI-encoded payload. The Axelar network verifies the payment "
"and relays it\n"
"      to the Sidechain, where the Amplifier gateway approves the message "
"and a relayer\n"
"      executes the call on the target contract."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The verifiers themselves are Amplifier participants who post a bond\n"
"      (50,000 AXL on mainnet) and register support for specific chains "
"via an\n"
"      <code>xrpl-handler</code> binary. The set above is what XRPL "
"mainnet sees today;\n"
"      the observed quorum sits at roughly two thirds of total signer "
"weight, which is\n"
"      the safety property — not the verifier count itself. When the set "
"rotates,\n"
"      it shows up here as a new <code>SignerListSet</code> transaction on"
" the gateway\n"
"      account, recorded in the timeline above."
msgstr ""

